# SolPoker configuration.
#
# Every value here is OPTIONAL. The defaults in src/lib/constants.ts point at
# public devnet infrastructure and the app runs without this file at all. Copy
# it to .env.local only when you want to override something, and set the same
# values in your Vercel project for production.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables exist here, which means every one of them is
# baked into the browser bundle and visible to anyone who opens devtools. Never
# put a private key, an API secret, or anything else you would not print on the
# page into this file. The app needs no secrets: players sign with their own
# wallets and the program is public on chain.


# --- The Solana base layer -----------------------------------------------
#
# Where accounts live between hands: buying chips, sitting down, cashing out,
# and the lobby and leaderboard listings.
#
# The default is MagicBlock's public devnet endpoint, which is fine for trying
# things out but rate-limits under real traffic. The lobby and the leaderboard
# both call getProgramAccounts, which public endpoints throttle hard, so if
# tables or the leaderboard start coming up empty for other people this is the
# first thing to change.
#
# Get a dedicated devnet URL free from either:
#   Helius     https://dashboard.helius.dev   (create an app, copy the devnet URL)
#   QuickNode  https://dashboard.quicknode.com (create a Solana devnet endpoint)
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC=https://devnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY


# --- The private rollup (TEE) --------------------------------------------
#
# Where hands are actually played, inside the Intel TDX enclave that keeps hole
# cards hidden. This is MagicBlock infrastructure; you do not host it, and
# there is no alternative endpoint to point at today.
#
# Change these only if MagicBlock gives you a different URL. The two must
# always name the same host: the first is used for transactions, the second for
# the subscriptions that make the table update live.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TEE_URL=https://devnet-tee.magicblock.app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TEE_WS=wss://devnet-tee.magicblock.app


# --- Not configurable, on purpose ----------------------------------------
#
# The program id is NOT an environment variable. It is compiled into the
# vendored IDL in src/lib/idl/, twice, and once of those is a raw byte array
# used to derive the delegation accounts. Setting an id here that disagreed
# with the IDL would let tables be created and joined but make every attempt to
# start a hand fail, which is exactly the bug that took a while to find during
# the last redeploy. Change the program by rebuilding and re-vendoring the IDL,
# never by configuration.
